<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank sets cash reserve requirements.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank sets cash reserve requirements.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said it would set a compulsory cash reserve requirement for the money market at zero for the period from Dec 30 to Jan 02.</p>
<p>The compulsory cash reserve for commercial banks is one of several instruments the central bank uses to steer money market liquidity and short term interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
